WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.980
<b>EX-ARM Auction</b>

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:51.690
<b>Breaking</b>

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:51.690
<b>Explosion Off the Coast of Tokyo Bay Megafloat</b>

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:40.520
<i>Reporting live from the scene!</i>

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:44.860
<i>As you can see, the roads to the Megafloat 
have been sealed off due to the bomb,</i>

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:48.970
<i>and the Defense Force has set up blockades 
at the entrances to the Megabridge.</i>

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:51.690
You can feel the tension in the air!

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:58.730
Oh, great. First suicide bombers, now this.

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:01.540
Is that island cursed or something?

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:04.730
Is everyone here?

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:07.480
An EX-ARM auction?

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:13.210
Correct. This 'ere's an invitation 
we snagged off one of our informants.

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:16.650
People invited have been 
tempted by the EX-ARMs

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:21.040
and have converged at the Tokyo
Bay Megafloat from all across the globe.

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:23.450
Superintendent, who are these people?

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:24.880
I'll introduce you.

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:27.440
This is Captain Wanibuchi 
from Public Safety External Affairs 4.

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:29.230
And this is Lieutenant Miyabe.

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:30.280
Hello.

00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:32.820
Public Safety?

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:36.510
Hello. You must be Number 00.

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:38.810
How I've wanted to meet you!

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:41.910
H-Hey, don't touch me!

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:45.720
Why'd Public Safety get that intel before us?

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:50.670
I believe you were filled in, 
Superintendent Rokuoin Chikage.

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:55.350
We'll be investigating this case 
jointly with External Affairs 4.

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:57.150
Are you kidding me?

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:59.030
No, no, that's not quite right.

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:03.700
You seem to have 
misunderstood something, Superintendent.

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:06.890
This isn't a joint investigation!

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:10.440
You'll be working under our command!

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:14.940
This is an order from the brass, 
to restore the credibility of the Japanese police!

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:18.880
You screwed up bad last time.

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:23.820
The brass is unanimous in the belief 
that you need some checks and balances.

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:27.160
And, of course, Chief Shiga has acquiesced.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:28.330
He what?!

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:29.240
Damn it!

00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:34.800
I don't care who's giving me orders 
as long as I can catch Beta.

00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:36.220
"Beta"?

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:40.790
Yeah. That guy who looks just like me.

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:44.120
I need to take him out.

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:46.830
I'm sure he was behind this bomb, too.

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:50.140
We'll get our hands on all the answers 
if we can catch him.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:54.120
Anyway, what do we gotta do?

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:58.870
You'll all take part 
in the casino auction undercover.

00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:01.910
Wait, me, too?

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:38.880
A showy island built with a casino 
to help the Tokyo Attack recovery efforts,

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:40.710
the Tokyo Megafloat,

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:45.130
<b>EX-ARM Auction Invite</b>

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:45.430
and an EX-ARM auction deliberately held there, eh?

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:50.730
How does it feel to be back home,

00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:53.380
Soma?

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:02.360
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:03.860
Well? Do you like it?

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:08.090
I like that I don't need anyone 
to carry me around anymore.

00:05:08.090 --> 00:05:11.640
The casino blocks off wireless comms 
to prevent cheating,

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:14.240
but your quantum network should work.

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:17.920
Keep us updated, 
and make sure you're not found.

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:21.900
If you're caught, 
you might get auctioned off.

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:23.530
Copy that.

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:28.540
Man, we gotta <i>work</i> at this casino?

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:33.420
A bomb just went off, 
but you wouldn't know it in here.

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:37.580
The people who chose to remain 
are probably really ballsy

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:39.310
or really frickin' crazy.

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:41.770
Where are Minami and Kondo?

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:45.860
They and Lieutenant Miyabe are acting 
as bodyguards for a certain group.

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:47.750
And who is that?

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:56.760
A political organization called Jinkoku-sha 
and its president, Hayama Gaho.

00:05:56.760 --> 00:06:01.300
He pulls all the strings in the Japanese economy 
without ever taking the spotlight.

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:04.340
This way, sir.

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:08.050
Oh, delivery from Akira.

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:13.720
Quickly identify and analyze the people 
attending the auction.

00:06:14.630 --> 00:06:18.600
This is Nguyen, from arms dealer Hanoi Farm!

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:21.780
And they're members of the Bathala smuggling ring.

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:26.550
I see Dario Goldoni from the Falcone Familia.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:32.650
The two in the back are Gina and Aristarif 
from Russian mafia group Spiritus.

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:36.300
Criminals everywhere you look.

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:40.860
Criminals from across the globe 
have gathered here for the EX-ARMs.

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:44.340
It's a golden opportunity to catch them all 
in one fell swoop.

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:47.060
The auction venue is this way.

00:06:47.560 --> 00:06:49.420
Let's go, Midori.

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:51.770
Yes, Grandfather.

00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:56.940
Hey! Watch where you're going!

00:06:58.180 --> 00:06:59.100
Al—

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:01.040
We're undercover, dumbass.

00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:02.020
But...

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:04.740
Are you all right, miss?

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:08.680
Oh, I'm fine. Thank you.

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:13.270
Take my hand, beautiful one.

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:20.170
Hey! Do you realize 
you're talking to an android?

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:24.570
And? All I care about is beauty, nothing else.

00:07:25.030 --> 00:07:26.640
Who even are you?

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:28.560
My name is Al Jarde.

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:30.760
Let us be on our way, Soma.

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:43.740
What's up?

00:07:44.450 --> 00:07:45.560
Nothing.

00:07:47.170 --> 00:07:51.690
Oh? Policemen guarding Jinkoku-sha?

00:07:51.690 --> 00:07:57.380
And they even sent in Number 00. 
The Japanese government is going all out.

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:05.060
<i>I hope you all enjoyed the show.</i>

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:14.890
<i>It's a pleasure to meet you. I'm Auctioneer.</i>

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:20.970
<i>Thank you very much for taking part 
in this EX-ARM auction.</i>

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:28.280
<i>Without further ado, let's take a look 
at the EX-ARM lineup available today.</i>

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:44.440
<i>Our first piece played a major role 
in the suicide bombings here on the Megafloat</i>

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:48.920
<i>and shook Japan to its very core. 
It's the EX-ARM that can turn people into bombs,</i>

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:51.030
<i>Number 9!</i>

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:57.470
<i>Next, the mystery EX-ARM that's making its way 
onto the market for the first time,</i>

00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:59.670
<i>Number 16!</i>

00:09:00.490 --> 00:09:03.390
<i>And finally, today's main attraction...</i>

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:10.940
<i>The legendary creation behind
the famous Tokyo Attack, Number 11!</i>

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:17.160
Man, what the hell? 
Is he its original wielder?

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:19.160
We don't know that.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:22.080
But he can't be projecting that hologram 
from too far away.

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:24.780
Auctioneer must be on this island.

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:32.350
<i>However, these three are the only EX-ARMs 
up for grabs.</i>

00:09:32.350 --> 00:09:35.470
<i>And while I realize this may be unreasonable,</i>

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:39.630
<i>I want to limit this auction 
to three bidders.</i>

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:46.180
<i>I'll let you all decide those three 
in any way you see fit.</i>

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:49.900
<i>Once you're down to three, 
we'll begin the auction,</i>

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:55.900
<i>and the highest bidder for each EX-ARM 
will go home with it.</i>

00:09:55.900 --> 00:09:59.660
<i>I wish you all the most wonderful EX-ARM.</i>

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:04.830
This is gonna turn out 
to be one nasty auction.

00:10:05.650 --> 00:10:07.530
Don't you get it?

00:10:07.530 --> 00:10:11.840
Auctioneer just told the participants 
to fight each other!

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:14.950
N-Number 11...

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:18.580
The demonic light that destroyed Japan.

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:23.480
I'll never forget that light 
I saw during the attack.

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:27.480
Its dark glow brought Japan to its knees!

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:31.760
We must seal it away forever 
by our own hands.

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:36.840
Letting criminal scum have it 
is out of the question!

00:10:37.330 --> 00:10:42.040
We must win all the EX-ARMs 
that are being auctioned off here.

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:44.680
It doesn't matter how much money it takes!

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:48.000
Make sure we win at all cos—

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:49.160
Grandfather!

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:51.290
Are you okay?

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:56.510
Crap. We need to go back to the hotel.

00:10:56.510 --> 00:10:57.840
G-Got it!

00:11:02.440 --> 00:11:05.780
Now, shall we begin?

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:14.810
The politicking between groups 
is about to start.

00:11:14.810 --> 00:11:16.410
This should be fun.

00:11:17.440 --> 00:11:21.110
Let me give you some advice. 
Join us, and we'll take out those guys.

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:25.280
I don't plan on working with anyone.

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:28.090
What, you wanna play lone wolf?

00:11:28.090 --> 00:11:31.760
We have an EX-ARM wielder, you know? 
You'll regret this.

00:11:31.760 --> 00:11:33.500
Shit, shit, shit, shit!

00:11:33.870 --> 00:11:37.550
And if <i>you</i> wish to oppose 
the people of the desert,

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:40.010
you'd best be ready to face the consequences.

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:44.230
Tch. Who does he think he is?

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:46.810
That's too bad.

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:51.720
If it's a business partner you want, 
I daresay I'll be a better fit.

00:11:58.210 --> 00:12:00.710
Man, what a shame.

00:12:01.220 --> 00:12:03.950
I'll welcome a signorina with open arms,

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:06.200
but I don't know about 
some random masked man.

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:17.880
My Number 23 is an EX-ARM 
that can materialize illusions.

00:12:23.400 --> 00:12:25.720
Okay, let's party!

00:12:30.430 --> 00:12:34.770
Unfortunately for you, 
Aristarif here has an EX-ARM.

00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:37.650
Play with us, and you'll get burned.

00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:41.270
Marvelous, Miss Gina.

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:44.940
I'm honored to work together with your team.

00:12:44.940 --> 00:12:47.340
Don't you have any troops?

00:12:48.510 --> 00:12:50.860
Oh, would you like to see them?

00:12:51.640 --> 00:12:55.080
I figured this would happen 
and made preparations.

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:02.380
There is absolutely no need for concern.

00:13:04.970 --> 00:13:06.970
<b>Illustration by Komi Shinya</b>

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:11.310
Is that girl gonna be okay?

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:13.160
I'm sure she will be.

00:13:13.160 --> 00:13:16.220
The president of Jinkoku-sha handpicked her.

00:13:16.220 --> 00:13:21.860
Uh, could you tell me more about Jinkoku-sha? 
I don't know anything about them.

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:26.420
Sure, but remember that 
this is only Public Safety's perspective.

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:28.870
After the 2020 Tokyo Attack,

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:32.570
which shattered the country's spine, 
what it needed most

00:13:32.570 --> 00:13:37.080
was an entity that commanded great financial 
and political power, even if illegally.

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:40.130
That situation helped Jinkoku-sha thrive.

00:13:41.780 --> 00:13:45.260
I hear they did some real bad shit 
to make it happen.

00:13:46.520 --> 00:13:52.090
Of course. No one could rise to power like that 
doing it the legal way.

00:13:52.090 --> 00:13:55.100
Honestly, there is so much dirt on them,

00:13:55.100 --> 00:14:00.710
it wouldn't be a surprise if anyone tried 
to off Jinkoku-sha and President Hayama.

00:14:04.120 --> 00:14:06.410
Does Midori know all this?

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:09.260
She absolutely does.

00:14:09.830 --> 00:14:13.990
She still has the composure 
to smile in this crazy situation.

00:14:14.480 --> 00:14:18.470
It shows that she understands the environment 
she was raised in.

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:25.640
How is the president doing?

00:14:25.640 --> 00:14:29.960
He got too agitated, 
and his chronic illness flared up.

00:14:29.960 --> 00:14:33.260
But he'll be fine if he takes
his medicine and gets some rest.

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:35.530
What about the auction, though?

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:37.980
No need to worry.

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:43.670
Grandfather said he's leaving the rest to me.

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:50.280
There's a lot I don't understand, 
so I hope you'll help me.

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:52.910
S-Sure...

00:14:52.910 --> 00:14:55.900
Okay, we'll keep you safe.

00:14:55.900 --> 00:14:58.250
Even if you're not exactly paragons of virtue,

00:14:58.250 --> 00:15:01.580
it's much better than letting
the others take Number 11.

00:15:02.050 --> 00:15:03.590
Akira.

00:15:04.950 --> 00:15:06.680
Get away from the windows!

00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:07.660
Alma?

00:15:07.660 --> 00:15:09.990
This hotel's been surrounded.

00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:14.220
Is that... Nguyen?

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:17.640
And Bathala. I see Spiritus, too.

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:20.060
They teamed up, huh?

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:23.790
Remember the cards placed
on the table in the auction hall?

00:15:23.790 --> 00:15:26.440
Look what they had written on the back.

00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:29.270
"I'll kill everyone 
who cooperates with Jinkoku-sha."

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:33.050
Wh-What do we do?

00:15:33.050 --> 00:15:34.970
We gotta get outta here.

00:15:34.970 --> 00:15:36.160
How?

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:37.790
The possible escape routes are...

00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:40.280
the hotel entrance and the parking lot.

00:15:40.280 --> 00:15:42.810
The enemy's probably there already.

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:45.840
Can the president escape, Midori?

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:48.460
He should be able to move, 
but we shouldn't push him.

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:50.480
Escaping won't be easy.

00:15:50.480 --> 00:15:52.000
What?

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:53.430
H-Hey.

00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:55.680
I have an idea.

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:56.560
What is it?

00:15:56.560 --> 00:15:59.190
Alma, Minami. Kiss for me.

00:16:01.090 --> 00:16:02.810
Wait, why now?

00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:05.040
Please do it! I need my powers!

00:16:05.040 --> 00:16:06.700
What is the meaning of this?

00:16:07.600 --> 00:16:09.320
Just do it already!

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:12.280
Oh, jeez! Fine!

00:16:14.560 --> 00:16:18.730
Genetic code confirmed. Key level 3 unlock.

00:16:20.290 --> 00:16:22.410
Here they come. Get ready.

00:16:24.470 --> 00:16:26.870
Wh-What's with them?

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:30.700
I took over the data links 
of the casino androids!

00:16:30.700 --> 00:16:32.420
Get outside now, guys!

00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:35.210
Move! Outta my way!

00:16:35.210 --> 00:16:37.470
Shit, they've been hacked!

00:16:40.280 --> 00:16:41.850
That was so exciting!

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:43.760
Nice idea, Akira!

00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:45.190
O-Oh, you know it.

00:16:45.190 --> 00:16:47.200
They'll be after us in no time! 
Let's get going!

00:16:47.200 --> 00:16:47.940
Okay!

00:16:48.300 --> 00:16:50.010
They just left the parking lot!

00:16:50.010 --> 00:16:52.490
Yes, I can see that.

00:16:52.490 --> 00:16:54.860
I suppose it's my turn now.

00:16:55.470 --> 00:16:57.570
We managed to escape somehow.

00:16:57.570 --> 00:16:59.560
We can't relax yet.

00:16:59.560 --> 00:17:00.200
Look ahead.

00:17:00.600 --> 00:17:02.000
Who's that?

00:17:02.320 --> 00:17:03.600
<i>Go around him!</i>

00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:04.460
Yeah!

00:17:19.940 --> 00:17:21.920
Those cars crashed into nothing at all.

00:17:21.920 --> 00:17:23.690
Damn, how about weapons?

00:17:33.110 --> 00:17:35.840
H-He stopped the bullets?

00:17:35.840 --> 00:17:38.620
Okay, yeah, he's got an EX-ARM.

00:17:40.840 --> 00:17:41.870
Kondo!

00:17:43.640 --> 00:17:45.070
I'm okay.

00:17:45.070 --> 00:17:47.170
Alma and I will hold him off.

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:52.040
Let's do this, Akira.

00:17:52.040 --> 00:17:52.940
Yeah!

00:17:58.390 --> 00:17:59.310
Now!

00:17:59.310 --> 00:18:01.050
Go, Minami!

00:18:06.040 --> 00:18:07.100
Not so fast.

00:18:13.020 --> 00:18:13.820
Alma!

00:18:15.330 --> 00:18:16.540
Damn it!

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:20.430
You okay, Alma?!

00:18:20.430 --> 00:18:22.530
Yes, but...

00:18:25.140 --> 00:18:26.480
He seems to be fine, too.

00:18:26.480 --> 00:18:29.250
Seriously? Just what is he?

00:18:29.990 --> 00:18:32.410
I am so moved.

00:18:32.410 --> 00:18:36.440
I'm amazed you could do that 
to let your friends escape.

00:18:37.030 --> 00:18:39.760
A beautiful display of selflessness.

00:18:42.230 --> 00:18:45.470
What's with these things? Are they androids?

00:18:46.400 --> 00:18:49.320
My kitties are quite feral, you see.

00:18:49.320 --> 00:18:53.720
They'll be taking both you 
and that mysterious EX-ARM wielder out.

00:18:57.950 --> 00:18:59.030
Shit!

00:18:59.670 --> 00:19:02.110
Akira, go after Minami and the rest.

00:19:02.720 --> 00:19:06.360
It's always been my role 
to act as a sacrificial lamb for humans.

00:19:06.360 --> 00:19:08.470
I'll be the eyes on the back of your head.

00:19:09.060 --> 00:19:10.540
We're squadmates.

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:12.380
I won't leave you alone!

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:34.550
Alma!

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:37.020
I'm sorry, Akira.

00:20:37.020 --> 00:20:40.690
My actuator's been damaged. 
I don't think I can move.

00:20:40.690 --> 00:20:42.880
Crap, this is bad.

00:20:47.080 --> 00:20:51.390
Sorry, Alma. I've got an idea, 
though it's do-or-die.

00:20:51.390 --> 00:20:54.620
I believe in you, Akira.

00:20:54.620 --> 00:20:55.900
We're squadmates.

00:20:57.640 --> 00:20:58.710
Go!

